The '''1997 UEFA Champions League final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match played at the [[Olympiastadion (Munich)|Olympiastadion]] in Munich on 28 May 1997 to determine the winner of the [[1996–97 UEFA Champions League]]. The match was contested by [[Borussia Dortmund]] of Germany and defending champions [[Juventus FC|Juventus]] of Italy. Borussia Dortmund won 3–1 with goals from [[Karl-Heinz Riedle]] and [[Lars Ricken]]; Juventus' only goal was scored by [[Alessandro Del Piero]]. This was the third from three consecutive finals featuring the defending champions, all of whom lost to their opponents.

==Route to the final==
{{further|1996–97 UEFA Champions League}}

In their first semi-final in Europe's premier tournament since [[1963–64 European Cup#Semi-finals|1964]], Dortmund defeated [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]], who themselves had not reached that stage since [[1968–69 European Cup#Semi-finals|1969]].

In the other half of the draw, Juventus easily overcame [[AFC Ajax|Ajax]], the same team they had beaten on penalties in the [[1996 UEFA Champions League final|previous year's final]].

